        <p>THERE'S NOTHING HALF SO SWEET IN LIFE AS LOVE'S YOUNG DREAM.—o sang Tom Moore years ago, and everyone who has been fortunate enough to consummate a happy engagement by a suitable marriage will, doubtless, cordially endorse this statement. What could be pleasanter than to be the proud possessor of a nice home, presided over by a loving, winsome wife, whose sole desire is to maga things comfortable for you and the little ones—when they arrive? Especially do you realise the charm when you know that, thanks to your own Industry and the economical rdethode of the aforesaid good lady, the "nest egg" at the bank is steadily augmenting.</p>
        <p>AGREEABLE HOME SURROUNDINGS, of course, tend to heighten the felicity, whilst upholding the family dignity. Good furnishings, artistically and sub- stantially constructed and tastefully arranged, not only give pleasure to all beholders, but have an educational, an elevat- ing influence upon the children, create in their susceptible minds the desire to possess a similarly furnished borne some day, supplied by the same good old Firm their parents patro- nised, make them frugal and timifty, so that when they reach manhood or womanhood other good orders are given to PITTS'S, of LONDON-ROAD, and GAYTHORN, who fulfil them in a satisfactory manner as usual.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S CELEBRATED HOUSES OF FURNl- tura at 15i, 221, 281, 38i, 50,75,100, 20.., up to 1,000 guineas, are in point of Excellence, Durability, and VALUE the VERY BEST OBTAINABLE. They represent a CLEAR SAVING OF 50 PER CENT, as compared with others. Full particulars and ILLUSTRATED FURNISHING GUIDE. containing 800 designs, priced, on application. Cash prices only quoted. Deferred payments 10 per cent. extra.</p>
