      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-03-27_WidnesExaminer_art0060" n="art0060">
        <head>TIIE CLERICS REIIIIINERATION.</head>
        <p>TIIE CLERICS REIIIIINERATION.</p>
        <p>Mr Mclntyre said they tied had betore them that morning the qu.stion of the clerk's remuneration for the past year and it was unanimously resolved that he receive £lOO for his ,iervicps. Tao excrss were little or nothing and he bad not re quired anything extra. Mr Woodward seconded, and tho resoluiou was approved. •</p>
        <p>THE HALF-YEARLY CONTRACTS. The clerk reported that tno 101 owing contrac's had been accepted :—Groceries, Mr E Gregory, Runcorn ; butchers' meat, Mr B Singleton, Warrington ;fib, R Mellhurst, Limited, Grimsby ; milk, butter and eggs Mr F Weir, Vadtby ; clothiw, Mr T R Wright, Halton; drapery, Mr T A Lee, Warrington : hoots, Mr J W Bazley, RuLcorn ; coal, R E vacs and Company. Limited ; "coke, Frddsham gas and water company ; coffin, Mr IT Barrow, Balton ; catt.ge, Mr W Grounds, Aston ; funerals, r Booth and Son, Runcorn; drysaltery. Mr D Gibson,Runcotn. Mr Woociward, in moving the adoption of the con- tracts, said he thought he only expressed the feeling of evnyone when he said that the new method of taking the contracts was a great improvement upon the old. Each feontract received the attenticn of each of the I committee and there was no possibility of any member of the committee being uninformed on the contract under consideration. Some of the tenders had fobs rejected on the ground that they had not complied with the instructions. They had not even had their attention. The Chairman asked whether any intimation would be sect to such persons telling them the reason ? Mr Woodward replied that he hoped the unsuccessful contractors would sec through the press that their ten- ders had not been considered lxicause they had not corn plied with the instructions. Mr Piling seconded and the contracte. were adopted' The Chairman rernarkind that the new system was great saving of time to the Board._</p>
      </div>
