      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-03-27_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>LANCASHIRE SENIOR COMPETITION</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE SENIOR COMPETITION</p>
        <p>'WARRINGTON AND THE CORONATION.</p>
        <p>The Mayor and the Proposed Subsidy</p>
        <p>from the Corporation.</p>
        <p>- - It will be remembered that at the meeting of inhabit- ants called to discuss the commemoration of the Coron- ation of Hine Edward VIII, a suggestion was made by' Alderman Shaw Grern that the Corporation should vote I a, certain sum to the Mayor towards the extra expenses which the commemoration of the event would entail. The suggestion met with unanimous approval. Last week, the Mayor addressed the following letter to Alderman Shaw Green Town Hall, Warrington, March 17th, 1902. Dear Mr Shaw Green, with reference to your suggestion at our firet Coronation meeting that the Couacil should be asked to vote a subsidy to the Mayor to supplement the voluntary subscriptions I should like to say that it would be extremely gratifying to me personally if this could be dispensed with and if the contributions re- ceived should be sufficient to defray the celebration expenses without infringing upon the rates.—Yours faithfully, J. CHARLTON PARR. An appeal for contributiOns has been addressed to the inhabitauts durine the past week. Elm Worship the Mayor has headed the list pith a subscription of £3OO. A list of subscriptions will be found in our advertising coluinns.it will be seen that the total amount promised Is now £5ll.</p>
        <p>Fire Brigade Test at Sankey Bridges. The Fire Brigade turned out on Saturday after- noon' for the purpose of testing the supply of water in case a fire should break out at the offices and other premises of Messrs Monks, Halt and com- pany's works, at Atherton's Quay. The members of the Fire grigine C mmittee present were coun- cillor Smethurst (chairman), and Councillors Bur- toc, A J Jolley, James Evans and Malkin. On the whole, the test,'which was a very searching one. was satisfactory, but the chairman expressed the opinion that when the tide was low there would be a scarcity of water for that part of the works nearest the town.</p>
        <p>• TnEBoAr Rana.—Thia annual event resulted in a win fnr Cambridge. Time as taken by Bensnn's Chronograph 19inius 9sec. Time last year 22m1n5 Slam.</p>
